# The Amazon S3-compatible object storage service (services/s3/,
# .kiro/specs/s3-compatible-storage/). Sourced from the top-level Kconfig's
# "Service Modules" menu.

config S3
	bool "Amazon S3-compatible object storage service"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/s3/ module: an Amazon S3-compatible object
	  store that unmodified AWS SDKs, the AWS CLI, rclone and Mountpoint
	  for Amazon S3 can point at, with object metadata in Kythira's Raft
	  groups and object bytes in content-addressed chunks outside the
	  Raft log. Service module number 8. s3_gateway_node runs any of
	  the four layers (gateway, front_end, metadata, blobs) a node is
	  given in KYTHIRA_S3_ROLES, co-located by default; --help lists
	  its settings. OpenSSL is needed for
	  SigV4, chunk digests and server-side encryption. Off by default
	  like every new module (services/README.md). See
	  .kiro/specs/s3-compatible-storage/.
